}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Anji Yukyuzan CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
A run of the mill, albeit very decent anti-Red/Floating nuker. Anji Yukyuzan has an effective damage per attack cycle of 224,400 against targets at Lv.30, (356,400 at Lv.50), though his damage is split between the main [[Omni Strike]] and its subsequent [[Wave Attack]], not to mention the fact that his damage is halved for enemies not hit by his Single Attack. This Wave Attack has very high pierce, hitting well into the backline at enemies like [[Professor A.]] without so much as breaking a sweat. He protects himself in a roundabout way via [[Knockback]]s which can trigger twice assuming targets weren't already staggered by the first hit. All of these qualities work together to make him a reliable Waver who can keep enemies like [[Baron Seal]] and [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants at bay even whilst dealing with untargeted enemies.

Anji's natural bulk is on the higher end too, letting him endure a good amount of punishment before getting knocked back. Enemies like [[Hannya]] will take a good amount of damage before shaking him off, aiding you immensely throughout the entire confrontation, usually getting more than your money's worth by the time Anji does die. However, make no mistake, he cannot facetank much of anything reliably even at higher levels. So, like all nukers, protect him well and he'll pay dividends. Additionally, [[Immune to Weaken]] has decent applicability against [[Calamary]], [[Puffzerker]], [[Cli-One]], [[Great Angel Chibinel]], and the aforementioned Hannya. [[Immune to Knockback]] is mainly useful against [[Mr. Mole]]. His only real weakness is his below-average DPS vs. grouped targets due to his Single Attack, although his high pierce and Knockback do leave an impact on the field regardless of who's targeted. 

{{Job|Classification = Nuker & Waver}}

